# Mark the moment (#551; written before the implementation): on the simulated Index, the moment BOTH trackpads are
# down the game marks it at once - no hold (the owner, 2026-10-20) - writing a marker folder <user dir>\marks\<utc>-<n>\
# (left.png, right.png, recorder.txt, clip.vrsim, meta.txt; note.wav when the voice note is on and a microphone
# recorded one) and showing "Moment marked (#N)" in the hero-dialogue panel (the subtitle panel of #460 / D-055) for
# about 2 s. One trackpad alone: no mark; the other pressed 1 s later: the mark then. Held on: no second mark; one let
# go and pressed again: the second mark. Both stick clicks held: no mark and no game menu (the D-058 fallback stays
# removed; menu-long-press.xrs has the radial's way to the menu). The feature's one CI sequence (coordinator Tests and
# CI rule 11), about 14 s after the load. Last, with the voice note on: a quick press of both marks and records no note.
#
# Assumes (the worker adds them, named exactly; tests/vr/MarkMomentTest.h has the whole interface):
#   marks.count          (count)  marks written since the start
#   marks.last           (text)   the last mark's folder name: <yyyymmdd>T<hhmmss>Z-<n> (UTC, n = its number)
#   marks.lastFiles      (text)   the non-empty files in it, sorted by name, joined by "," without spaces
#   marks.recording      (bool)   a voice note records now (only while both trackpads are held)
#   marks.noteMs         (number) how long it records so far, ms; 0 when none records
#   marks.note           (bool)   the voice note is on (cfg.ini vr_mark_note; the channel's `marks note on|off`)
#   marks.gesture        (text)   both.trackpad on the Index, none on a controller without trackpads (the Touch)
#   scene.subtitle.notice (text)  the notice the hero-dialogue panel shows: none | marked | recording | saved
#   log "[vr] mark #<n>: marks\<folder> files=<lastFiles>" once the folder is written, and the panel's
#   "vr.scene.subtitle notice=<marked|recording|saved> ... text="<the line>"" when a notice shows
# The voice note is off for steps 1-5: CI runs on the owner's PC, where a microphone may be plugged in (a room
# recording must never land in a CI user directory); the note itself is a host test (tests/vr/VoiceNoteTest.h) and
# the owner's headset test. Step 6 turns it on for a press too short to keep anything.
@sim idle
@save mvp-new-game
@args --loadslot 0

@until state eq GAMEPLAY 60s
@until vr.sim.timelineFrame ge 270 60s       # 3 s into the level: past its fade-in (TRAPS.md)
@assert player.controlsBlocked eq false
@assert vr.input.controllers eq index
@assert menuMode eq ingame
@assert marks.count eq 0
@assert marks.gesture eq both.trackpad
@assert marks.noteMs eq 0
@assert scene.subtitle.notice eq none
marks note off
@frames 2
@assert marks.note eq false

# 1. Both stick clicks held 2.5 s: nothing special - no mark, no game menu (past the removed fallback's 2 s)
vr-input down left.stick_click; vr-input down right.stick_click
@wait 2500
@assert marks.count eq 0
@assert menuMode eq ingame
vr-input up left.stick_click; vr-input up right.stick_click
@wait 300
@assert marks.count eq 0
@assert scene.subtitle.notice eq none
@assert menuMode eq ingame

# 2. The left trackpad alone for 1 s: no mark. The right pressed too: the mark at once, its confirmation in the
# hero-dialogue panel (below the view centre: the hero's panel)
@mark
vr-input down left.trackpad
@wait 1000
@assert marks.count eq 0
@assert scene.subtitle.notice eq none
vr-input down right.trackpad
@until marks.count eq 1 1s
@until scene.subtitle.notice eq marked 1s
@assert scene.subtitle.visible eq true
@assert scene.subtitle.drawn eq chest
@assert marks.recording eq false
@assert menuMode eq ingame

# 3. Both held on: the confirmation stays about 2 s and goes; no second mark (the note is off: nothing records)
@wait 1000
@assert scene.subtitle.notice eq marked
@assert scene.subtitle.panel eq true
@until scene.subtitle.notice eq none 2s
@wait 500
@assert marks.count eq 1
@assert marks.recording eq false
@assert marks.noteMs eq 0

# 4. The right let go and pressed again (the left still held): the second mark, at once
vr-input up right.trackpad
@wait 300
@assert marks.count eq 1
vr-input down right.trackpad
@until marks.count eq 2 1s
@until scene.subtitle.notice eq marked 1s
vr-input up left.trackpad; vr-input up right.trackpad
@wait 300
@assert marks.count eq 2
@assert menuMode eq ingame

# 5. The folders: the five files, written and not empty; no voice note (off). The log has the first confirmation's
# line and the first folder's, in either order (the files may be written after the confirmation shows): one look-ahead
# for each; then the second folder's line
@until marks.lastFiles eq clip.vrsim,left.png,meta.txt,recorder.txt,right.png 10s
@assert marks.recording eq false
@log (?s)^(?=.*vr\.scene\.subtitle notice=marked [^\n]*text="Moment marked \(#1\)")(?=.*\[vr\] mark #1: marks\\\d{8}T\d{6}Z-1 files=clip\.vrsim,left\.png,meta\.txt,recorder\.txt,right\.png) 5s
@log \[vr\] mark #2: marks\\\d{8}T\d{6}Z-2 files=clip\.vrsim,left\.png,meta\.txt,recorder\.txt,right\.png 5s

# 6. The voice note on (push-to-talk): a press of both let go at once - the mark, and no note: the note records only
# while both are held and keeps nothing shorter than 0.3 s (VoiceNote::minMs), so the result is the same with or
# without a microphone on the machine (no microphone: no note, no error). Nothing records once they are up, and the
# panel shows no "Note saved" (notice saved) - only the mark's own confirmation
marks note on
@frames 2
@assert marks.note eq true
@assert marks.noteMs eq 0
@mark
vr-input down left.trackpad; vr-input down right.trackpad
@frames 2
vr-input up left.trackpad; vr-input up right.trackpad
@until marks.count eq 3 2s
@frames 5
@assert marks.recording eq false
@assert marks.noteMs eq 0
@assert scene.subtitle.notice ne recording
@wait 1000
@assert marks.recording eq false
@assert scene.subtitle.notice ne saved
@assert marks.lastFiles eq clip.vrsim,left.png,meta.txt,recorder.txt,right.png
@nolog vr\.scene\.subtitle notice=(recording|saved)
@log \[vr\] mark #3: marks\\\d{8}T\d{6}Z-3 files=clip\.vrsim,left\.png,meta\.txt,recorder\.txt,right\.png 10s
@assert errors eq 0
